ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi152: Single ADVANCED_FACE on a PLANE in a CLOSED_SHELL; outer EDGE_LOOP has 4 edges: E0 LINE P0=(0,0,0)→P1=(10,0,0); E1 CIRCLE arc center=(0,0,0) radius=10, P1=(10,0,0)→P2=(0,10,0), theta=0→pi/2; E2 LINE P2=(0,10,0)→P3=(3,3,0) — intersects arc E1 near theta=pi/3; E3 LINE P3=(3,3,0)→P0=(0,0,0) — closes loop; LINE E2 crosses CIRCLE arc E1 inside the domain; FixIntersectingEdges split logic applies linear parameter interpolation to arc parameter — non-linear arc maps linearly-interpolated parameter to wrong 3D split point IS mechanism; EDGE_LOOP IS wired into FACE_OUTER_BOUND -> ADVANCED_FACE in CLOSED_SHELL; never orphaned */
HEADER;
